  "sq_pmc_resolution": {
    "status": "RESOLVED",
    "root_cause": "Attaching device_counting_service tens of seconds before the measured launch freezes the SQ-block counters at a constant for the whole megamoe window (deltas 0) while TCC/GRBM keep updating; the counters are alive before and after. Verified in pmc_back/{za,zb,pa7}: SQ_BUSY_CU_CYCLES max 15166971373, SQ_THREAD_CYCLES_VALU max 609733405630, SQ_VALU_MFMA_BUSY_CYCLES max 529633280, all frozen inside the window.",
    "fix": "Attach DCS exactly one launch before CAPTURE_INDEX with no host sleep (a host sleep desynchronises the 8 EP8 ranks and hangs the tail), 3 ms settle in the sampler thread, and pmc_stop() immediately after the capture so later timing rounds are unperturbed.",
    "evidence": "pmc/ja: SQ_BUSY_CU_CYCLES total_delta 272737818, in-window 8.0M-10.2M per ~74us; pmc/jb: SQ_VALU_MFMA_BUSY_CYCLES total_delta 166723584, in-window 0 -> 15.9M (GEMM1) -> 0 (tail). Both CAPTURE_RC=0, overflow_bits=0, Home_Combine=1024 slices, no latched device_error.",
    "retracted_claim": "The earlier 'neighbour job holds the SQ PMU' and 'gfx942 MFMA counters are dead under DCS' conclusions were WRONG and are retracted."
  },
  "compute_formula": "100 * SQ_VALU_MFMA_BUSY_CYCLES / (80 * GRBM_GUI_ACTIVE); the SKILL.md:64 constant 12.5 = 100/8 assumes 8 CUs, MI308X has 80, so the CU-count-correct factor is 100/80 = 1.25"
